When \(x=0\), \(u=2(0)+1=1\). When \(x=2\), \(u=2(2)+1=5\). Therefore the \(u\)-limits are \(1\) and \(5\), not \(0\) and \(2\). The correct integral is \[
\frac{1}{2}\int_1^5 u^2\,du=\frac{1}{2}\left[\frac{u^3}{3}\right]_1^5=\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{124}{3}=\frac{62}{3}
\]. The student failed to change the limits.
